immune polyglandular syndrome type 1, which involves multiple autoimmune disorders.", "ARNOLD A.:Arnold A. is an author who has contributed to the understanding of multiple endocrine neoplasia type 1 and its genetics.", "VALDÉS GALLEGO N.:Valdés Gallego N. is an author known for his contributions to the field of endocrinology and nutrition. He has authored a manual that focuses on endocrine neoplasia, with a specific emphasis on multiple endocrine neoplasia. His work in the \"Manual de Endocrinología y Nutrición\" highlights his expertise and dedication to advancing knowledge in these important areas of health.", "LITIASIS RENAL:LITIASIS RENAL, also known as kidney stones or renal lithiasis, is a medical condition characterized by the formation of solid mineral and salt deposits in the kidneys. This condition affects approximately 5-15% of the population and can lead to significant morbidity and healthcare costs. The formation of kidney stones can be influenced by various factors, including the concentration of solutes in the urine, dietary habits, hydration levels, and metabolic disorders. High calcium levels in the urine, hyperuricemia, and metabolic syndrome are also associated with the development of this condition. Litiasis renal can cause considerable pain and complications in health, making it a significant urological pathology that requires attention and management.", "HIPERPARATIROIDISMO:Hiperparatiroidismo es una alteración hormonal que puede afectar a pacientes con insuficiencia renal, influyendo en su nutrición. Esta condición, también conocida como hyperparathyroidism, es un trastorno que puede presentarse en individuos con enfermedad renal crónica, lo que requiere intervenciones nutricionales específicas para manejar sus efectos.", "D:D is a hypothetical patient who presents with symptoms and a medical history suggestive of Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1). In addition to being a clinical case study, D also serves as a response option in the context of the questions presented in the modules. This dual role highlights D's significance in both medical education and the understanding of MEN1.", "TNE:TNE refers to neuroendocrine tumors, which can be non-functioning and are often associated with MEN1.", "GASTRINOMAS:Gastrinomas are a type of neuroendocrine tumor characterized by the secretion of gastrin, a hormone that stimulates gastric acid production. These tumors are often located in the duodenum and are commonly associated with Zollinger-Ellison syndrome, a condition marked by excessive gastric acid secretion leading to recurrent peptic ulcers. Additionally, gastrinomas can be linked to Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), a genetic disorder that affects the endocrine glands.", "NEUROENDOCRINE TUMOR:Neuroendocrine tumors (NETs) are a diverse group of tumors that originate from neuroendocrine cells, which are specialized cells that produce hormones. One specific type of neuroendocrine tumor is found in the pancreas, where it affects the hormone-producing cells, leading to significant health complications. These tumors can be associated with various syndromes, including Multiple Endocrine Neoplasia type 1 (MEN1), highlighting their complex nature and potential for systemic effects.", "ANALYTICS:Analytics refers to the medical tests and evaluations performed to assess the patient's condition, including hormone levels.", "MACROADENOMA HIPOFISARIO:Macroadenoma hipofisario refers to a large pituitary adenoma that produces prolactin, commonly seen in patients with MEN1."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}